WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.112
At scale, let policy do it.

2
00:00:02.112 --> 00:00:04.816
The Cloud Adoption Framework's pattern,

3
00:00:04.816 --> 00:00:08.750
Private Link and D N S integration
at scale, has three parts.

4
00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:12.087
Deny private link zones in
workload subscriptions.

5
00:00:12.087 --> 00:00:14.276
Deny pass with public endpoints.

6
00:00:14.276 --> 00:00:18.825
And a deploy-if-not-exists policy that
adds the zone group in the central zone.

7
00:00:18.825 --> 00:00:21.156
The Azure landing zones initiative,

8
00:00:21.156 --> 00:00:24.730
Configure Azure pass services
to use private D N S zones,

9
00:00:24.730 --> 00:00:28.459
carries the built-in definitions,
and the policy's managed

10
00:00:28.459 --> 00:00:32.188
identity needs Private D N S
Zone Contributor on the zones.

11
00:00:32.188 --> 00:00:36.876
This prevents a danger the guide
lists: zones in workload subscriptions

12
00:00:36.876 --> 00:00:41.563
split records across zones, and
resolution fails or quietly goes public.

13
00:00:41.563 --> 00:00:46.231
The rollout follows the usual pattern:
the deny policies in audit first,

14
00:00:46.231 --> 00:00:48.922
with Module 1's public pass list reviewed,

15
00:00:48.922 --> 00:00:52.850
then public access off per
resource, then the deny policies.
